# Never send the host's node_modules/dist into the build context — every
# stage in Dockerfile installs/builds its own inside the container (see the
# `build` and `runtime` stages' `npm ci` / `npm ci --omit=dev` / `npm run
# build`). Copying host artifacts in here would risk the exact "npm ci run
# on the host, node_modules copied into the image" mistake the Dockerfile is
# careful to avoid for `sharp`'s native binary (built for the HOST's
# platform, not necessarily linux/amd64 inside the container).
node_modules
dist

.git
*.md
deno.lock
npm-debug.log*

# NOTE: `test/` is intentionally NOT excluded here. The Dockerfile's
# `runtime` stage does `COPY test/fixtures/minimal.tex test/fixtures/
# minimal.tex` for the priming/smoke-test compile — Docker's .dockerignore
# applies to every COPY/ADD (not just implicit context), so excluding the
# whole `test/` directory here would break that explicit COPY too. The
# Dockerfile never does a broad `COPY . .` in `runtime`, so `test/`'s other
# contents (unit test files, other fixtures) are simply never copied into
# the runtime image regardless of what's listed here.
